cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this proof using the metadata below and identify the commit consulted."
title: "Real-Rootedness of Three Consecutive Eulerian Polynomials"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Ozols
    given-names: Chris
    website: "https://github.com/cozuya"
url: "https://github.com/cozuya/eulerian-three-term-real-rootedness"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cozuya/eulerian-three-term-real-rootedness"
abstract: >-
  A Lean-checked proof that for fixed real b, c >= 0 the polynomials
  A_n(x) + b A_(n-1)(x) + c A_(n-2)(x), where A_n is the Eulerian polynomial,
  have only real roots for every n >= 3 if and only if c <= b^2/4 + b + 3.
  Repeated roots are allowed and the boundary is included; necessity comes
  from n = 3. The region strictly contains the sufficient region of
  Athanasiadis (On the real-rootedness of the Eulerian transformation,
  Example 3.3). The proof uses Cayley coordinates, a positive-residue
  induction, a logarithmic-derivative inequality and a sign count at hybrid
  test points. By Chris Ozols, with AI-assisted proof development and
  formalization; the Lean formalization was written by Anthropic's Claude,
  with its final verification step completed by OpenAI's Codex. Verified with
  Lean 4.35.0 and Mathlib v4.35.0, using only the standard axioms propext,
  Classical.choice and Quot.sound. No claim of novelty, first discovery, or
  historical priority.
keywords:
  - Eulerian polynomials
  - real-rooted polynomials
  - linear combinations
  - interlacing
  - Cayley transform
  - partial fractions
  - Athanasiadis Example 3.3
  - Eulerian transformation
  - Lean
  - Mathlib
  - formal proof
